2026-11-01T10:36:26+00:00 session on m34 (the phone's matrix, session 3 (#27, #46, #47): the phone's equal-latency candidates past 640, B1 and B2 in FP32 at 800 against B3 and B4 in per-channel INT8 at 1120, each pair back to back; then B1 and B2 in FP32 at 960 (their INT8 speed-up, #47) and the pruned P2 and P4 in FP32 at 960; ONNX Runtime only, all 1,610 test-dev images; about 5 h with the fixed 3-minute start waits. Seed 1638 runs them by value, so a cut takes the pruned cells first: the two pairs, the FP32 cells at 960, then the pruned cells): 8 cells; every run uses 4 threads and 20 warm-up images, untimed
